  "notes": [
    "This is the SDD section 49 item 1 preliminary load schedule. It is a priority and sequencing schedule, not an electrical schedule.",
    "No measured power, branch circuit, breaker number or circuit rating is invented. rated_power_kw is null for every record and every unknown is listed in open_fields, consistent with the 'deliberately unresolved' section of the package README.",
    "estimated_power_kw is populated only where the asset register already carried a planning baseline (control core 0.25 kW, server rack 1.5 kW). It is a planning figure, not a measurement; data_status records that.",
    "base_tier uses the SDD 31.2 zero-based tier model. The asset register property load_tier is one-based (Tier 0 -> load_tier 1), so base_tier = register load_tier - 1 for all twelve loads.",
    "measured_power_point names the canonical point that will carry the measurement once the binding is commissioned. The binding for every one of these points is still 'tbd' in data/point_bindings.yaml, so a load is not confirmed shed until that point reports (SDD 32.2).",
    "restart.delay_s, inrush_class, minimum_on_time_s and minimum_off_time_s are commissioning parameters with engineering defaults: compressors and submersible pumps get the anti-short-cycle 300 s off time, lamp loads get a restrike allowance, and electronics get short values. Every one of them is also listed in open_fields.",
    "Groups S5 and S8 have no member in this revision. S5 needs branch-circuit identification before nonessential Tier 2 branches can be named; S8 is an equipment-native emergency procedure and is deliberately not automated.",
    "shed.action values are supervisory intents: never_shed, stop, reduce, local_survival_profile, graceful_shutdown, deny_new_grants and revoke_lease. The EMS requests them; the local controller enforces equipment interlocks (SDD 30.4).",
    "Tier 0 loads carry shed.permitted false and no shed_group. The shedding engine also refuses Tier 0 independently, so a data error in this file cannot shed physical protection."
